question 7	Determine the cumulative time complexity (Big-Oh) for the following expressions: (3 marks) 
a.	O(n log(n)) + O(n) 
Between O(n log(n)) and O(n), n log(n) grows Much Faster than n. O(n) becomes insignificant for n. Therefore, the cumulative time complexity is O(n log(n))

b.	O(n) + O(log(n)) 
The cumulative time complexity of O(n) + O(log(n)) is  O(n), since O(n) is significantly Bigger than O(log(n))

c.	O(log(n)) + O(1)
In this case, the cumulative time complexity is O(log n). because log n grows faster than constant 1.



